{"n": 64, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "64.webp", "text": "11-36\n\nLogsen mounting bolt on camshaft\nsprocket.\n\nLoosen nut on tensioning roller.and\ntake off toothed drive belt.\n\nNote:\n\nAlways replaced an used toothed drive\nbelt after loosening the tensioning\nroller, regardless of the mileage.\n\nInstalling and Tightening Toothed\nDrive Belt:\n\nPull off vent hose, unscrew bolts and\ntake off cylinder head cover,\n\nInstallation:\n\nCheck gasket, replacing If necessary.\nTighten bolts crosswise from inside to\noutside.\n\nTightening tarque = 9 Nm (6.5 ft. Ibs.).\n\nRemove camshaft cover (1)\n\n40 11138\n\ninstallation\n\nHold camshaft in TDC position (vaives\nof cylinder no. 4 overlap) with Special\nTool 11 3 190.\n\nBolt on camshaft sprocket with an\nInitial torque of 1 to 3 Nm (0.7 to 2.1 ft.\nIbs.) so that It can still be turned with-\nout play and turn In engine's direction\nof rotation against the stop*(tab In\ngroove).\n\nMount tensioning roller that It can still\nbe tumed with a slight tightening\ntorque of approx. 1 Nm (0.7 ft. Ibs.).\n\nMount toothed drive belt while pulling\nfrom the crankshaft sprocket to the\ntensioning roller.\n\nCenter toothed drive beit on the cam-\nshaft sprocket.\n\nPreparing Special Tool 11 2 080 for\nMeasuring Tightness (also Refer to\nOperating Instructions for 11 2 080):\n\nPull up lockpin (1) and move bearing\npins to maximum opening width with\nslide (2).\n\nSet dial gage needle to “0” and line up\ndrag needle with the gage needle.\nApply tester on toothed drive belt in\nSuch a manner that the center bearing\npin (3) bears In one of the teeth gaps.\n\nPush In slide (2) until engagment of\nthe lockpin Is noticed and adjust the\ntoothed drive belt's tightness by\nturning the tensioning roller (4).\nSpecification: 32 + 2 scale graduations.\nTighten the tensioning roller with 22\nNm (16 ft. Ibs.) and the camshaft\nsprocket with 63 Nm (46 ft. Ibs.) torque.", "words": [["11-36", 0.4661, 0.0332, 0.5203, 0.057], ["Logsen", 0.2